WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:01.590
Okay.

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:08.140
I want to have an adult conversation with
you about whether strategically it is time

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:15.550
for Bernie Sanders to start attacking Elizabeth
Warren hard if he wants to maintain a shot

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:17.550
at securing the democratic nomination.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.850
Now stop it.

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:24.220
Delete that email draft you've already opened
to me where you're about to rip me a new one.

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:25.990
I want to be really clear here.

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:28.279
This is a strategic conversation.

00:00:28.279 --> 00:00:31.060
I'm against toxic democratic infighting.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:35.950
I believe that we need to be running good
issue-based campaigns, but it is now been

00:00:35.950 --> 00:00:41.070
brought up to me several times and I want
to address it on the fact to answer the question,

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:43.940
what can Bernie do to get back in this race?

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:45.630
We just looked at polling data.

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:49.730
The polling data is not looking good for Bernie,
particularly over the last couple of weeks.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:53.730
Elizabeth Warren has taken a lead in an average
of recent polls and is trending.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:59.670
She is now nationally the front runner or
you could take co front runner with Joe Biden.

00:00:59.670 --> 00:01:01.660
Bernie Sanders had a heart procedure.

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:03.270
He's been off the trail for a little bit.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:06.740
He's getting back to it, but it has hurt his
poll numbers.

00:01:06.740 --> 00:01:11.600
I wish it were different, but this is the
reality that we're dealing with and so I started

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:18.210
seeing messages like for example on our subreddit
where user Wes' NAZ posted about this, who

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:23.880
said from start to present, the Sanders campaign
hasn't gone after Warren.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:25.869
I think this has been a smart move.

00:01:25.869 --> 00:01:29.220
Allowing them to be harder on more conservative
candidates.

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:34.380
However, it is my belief that the time is
now for Sanders to go on the offense.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:35.579
Here is my case.

00:01:35.579 --> 00:01:37.740
Only three candidates remain in double digit
polling.

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.320
No one else has a chance.

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:42.149
Number two, Bernie just had heart surgery.

00:01:42.149 --> 00:01:44.530
He needs to retake control of the race.

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:46.989
Number three, Bernie's polling has been leveling
off.

00:01:46.989 --> 00:01:50.179
He needs to take out Warren and get her supporters.

00:01:50.179 --> 00:01:53.619
Number four, he raised more than anyone else
in the third quarter of the year.

00:01:53.619 --> 00:01:59.559
He has a strong following and number five,
Warren has been given way too much easy air

00:01:59.559 --> 00:02:01.799
time, and she isn't left enough.

00:02:01.799 --> 00:02:04.549
She won't make the changes that Bernie will.

00:02:04.549 --> 00:02:10.009
I think Warren's presence has been a benefit
for the country, but now she needs to go.

00:02:10.009 --> 00:02:11.650
So here's what you have to understand.

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:14.709
This is a strategic analysis.

00:02:14.709 --> 00:02:17.459
Imagine that Bernie doesn't go after Warren,
right?

00:02:17.459 --> 00:02:21.260
Say Bernie doesn't take the advice from Wes'
NAS and says, I'm not going to attack Warren.

00:02:21.260 --> 00:02:22.269
That's not been my strategy.

00:02:22.269 --> 00:02:23.640
I'm not going to do it.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:29.040
He goes into his next debate and he attacks
Joe Biden who he is very different from the

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:35.109
problem is that any damage Bernie is able
to do to Joe Biden helps Elizabeth Warren

00:02:35.109 --> 00:02:36.450
as much as it helps him.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:37.989
Why do I say that?

00:02:37.989 --> 00:02:40.189
Because mathematically that's the reality.

00:02:40.189 --> 00:02:47.420
If you look at second choices for Biden voters,
30% of Biden voters would switch to Warren.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:52.790
If they abandoned Joe Biden and 25% of Biden
voters would switch to Bernie.

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:58.999
What this means is that when Biden loses support,
when a Biden supporter sees Bernie destroy

00:02:58.999 --> 00:03:04.540
Biden on the stage, they are marginally more
likely to switch their vote from Biden to

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:07.660
Warren than from Biden to Bernie.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:13.790
Mathematically, that means that going after
Biden is not particularly useful to Bernie

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:18.870
Sanders by successfully attacking Biden, by
making them look really bad.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:22.190
Bernie is helping Warren at least as much
as he helps himself.

00:03:22.190 --> 00:03:26.400
This is a mathematical reality, so this is
an important question.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:31.499
Is there a path to the nomination for Bernie
to get from the 1415 he's pulling on average

00:03:31.499 --> 00:03:33.950
right now to get into the lead?

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:41.310
That does not require taking support from
Elizabeth Warren in the most primitive mathematical

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:42.310
sense.

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:46.650
Yes, all of the other candidates, if you take
out from the a hundred percent right now,

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:51.090
you take out Biden's support and Warren support
and Bernie support.

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:55.909
Everybody else, like Buddha, judge or Rorick,
everybody, they have a total of 22% support.

00:03:55.909 --> 00:03:56.909
There's little slices.

00:03:56.909 --> 00:04:03.590
Buddha judge has 5.6 Andrew Yang is 2.8 Chelsea
Gabbert has 0.8 all together.

00:04:03.590 --> 00:04:08.749
That's 22% but Bernie can't get that full
22% right.

00:04:08.749 --> 00:04:12.650
Even if he obliterates every other candidate
and makes everybody say, I need to abandon

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:14.420
all of these people.

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:19.609
Bernie is only the preferred second option
for a slice of those candidates.

00:04:19.609 --> 00:04:26.210
So imagine that Bernie so brutally destroys
and embarrass as booted judge, that every

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:29.990
booted judge supporter says, I'm going to
my second choice.

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:33.690
Buddha judge supporters prefer Warren over
Bernie.

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:35.280
Same thing with Carla Harris.

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:38.680
Harris supporters prefer Warren over Bernie.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:39.930
So I hate this.

00:04:39.930 --> 00:04:44.110
I looked at this every which way last night
and this morning.

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:51.880
But mathematically, I don't see a way for
Bernie to win without taking support directly

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:58.250
from Elizabeth Warren, which is tough because
Elizabeth Warren supporters marginally prefer

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.349
Biden over Bernie.

00:05:00.349 --> 00:05:01.349
Okay?

00:05:01.349 --> 00:05:02.349
I don't want to see it.

00:05:02.349 --> 00:05:04.020
I don't want to see this get ugly.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:08.599
There may be intangible collateral damage
that are really ugly showdown between Bernie

00:05:08.599 --> 00:05:13.630
and Warren could due to the eventual candidate,
but I know that there are people in my audience

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:19.030
who do want to see it and believe that any
cost to get Bernie the nomination over Warren

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:20.030
is worth it.

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:24.660
Now, of course, that's not even this simple
because there's also the issue of whether

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:31.080
the people who would vote for Bernie would
be convinced to do it by seeing him attack

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:36.340
Elizabeth Warren, that may actually turn voters
off and it's not been Bernie strategy.

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:40.820
It could be anathema to the way that he has
run his campaign.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:43.330
So my question to you today is, we're being
adults here.

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:44.870
I'm not suggesting anyone do anything.

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:47.300
I'm just telling you what the math says.

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:48.300
Reply in the comments.

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:51.639
If you're watching on YouTube or send me a
tweet at D Pacman.

00:05:51.639 --> 00:05:58.139
Is there a way for Bernie Sanders to get back
in control here without going directly after

00:05:58.139 --> 00:05:59.139
Elizabeth Warren?

00:05:59.139 --> 00:06:00.139
Okay.

